    "https://belmontabbeycollege.edu/about-us/employment/chemistry-adjunct-position/": {
      "title": "Chemistry Adjunct Position",
      "description": "Chemistry Adjunct Position - Belmont Abbey College Skip to main content About Us About Us About Us Mission & vision Abbey News Leadership Monastery & Basilica Library Performing Arts Accreditation Belmont Abbey College The Catholic College of the South VISIT Academics Admissions APPLY GET INFO My abbey GIVE Chemistry Adjunct Position Home > About Us > Employment > Chemistry Adjunct Position Analytical Chemistry Adjunct Position Position Summary Belmont Abbey College invites applications for adjunct faculty to teach a day time, in person course in Analytical Chemistry in the spring of 2027. Job Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will include preparation, teaching, and assessment of students in an upper-level Analytical Chemistry lecture that meets 3 hours a week and a 3-hour lab that meets once a week. Qualifications Minimum of a Master’s degree in Chemistry or ABD, PhD preferred. Prior experience in college teaching is preferred. The ideal candidate must understand and embrace the responsibility of supporting the college’s Catholic identity and value participation in an academic community dedicated to a robust Catholic and Benedictine educational vision. Preference will be given to those candidates who can demonstrate a philosophy of teaching and research that fits well with the institution’s emphasis on the education of the whole person, and with the approach to education expressed in St. John Paul II’s Ex corde Ecclesiae. Application Process Fill out the following form to apply for one of Belmont Abbey College’s available academic positions. APPLY NOW To complete your application, mail or email a cover letter addressing your interest in the position and a statement describing how you see yourself supporting the College’s Catholic identity and values , CV, and names, addresses, and phone numbers of three references to: Dr. Heather Ayala Chair, Biology & Biochemistry Department Belmont Abbey College, Belmont, NC 28012. heatherayala@bac.edu A review of applications will begin immediately. Finalists will be required to submit official transcripts. Meet our Leadership Team Experienced, passionate and dedicated to the Benedictine spirit, the leadership team of the Abbey focuses on the academic, professional and spiritual growth of all students. See more Contact 100 Belmont-Mt. Holly Road Belmont, NC 28012 ADMISSIONS: 1-888-222-0110 FINANCIAL AID: 1-704-461-7000 MAIN NUMBER: 1-704-461-6700 FAX: 704-461-6220 info@bac.edu Quick Links DIRECTIONS TO THE COLLEGE SUPPORT THE COLLEGE TITLE IX CAMPUS DIRECTORY BELMONT ABBEY MONASTERY THE CATHOLIC SHOPPE CAMPUS SAFETY COLLEGE BOOKSTORE PRESS INQUIRIES ADMISSION INFORMATION VISIT CAMPUS MAP EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITIES PERFORMING ARTS 100 Belmont-Mt. Holly Road Belmont, NC 28012 ADMISSIONS: 1-888-222-0110 MAIN NUMBER: 1-704-461-6700 FAX: 704-461-6220 info@bac.edu Copyright ©2026 Belmont Abbey College | Minutes from Charlotte, we are ranked one of the top comprehensive colleges in the South by US News and World Report. Since 1876, the mission of Belmont Abbey College is the education of students from diverse religious, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds in the liberal arts tradition as guided by our catholic intellectual heritage and inspired by the 1500-year-old Benedictine monastic tradition. | Privacy Policy | Designed by Fuzati Copyright ©2026 Belmont Abbey College | Minutes from Charlotte, we are ranked one of the top comprehensive colleges in the South by US News and World Report. Since 1876, the mission of Belmont Abbey College is the education of students from diverse religious, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds in the liberal arts tradition as guided by our catholic intellectual heritage and inspired by the 1500-year-old Benedictine monastic tradition. | Privacy Policy | Designed by Fuzati Copyright ©2026 Belmont Abbey College | Privacy Policy | Designed by Fuzati Are you a current North Carolina High School student? YES! NO! EXPLORE ADMISSIONS × So that we can