    "https://belmontabbeycollege.edu/about-us/employment/motorsport-management-adjunct-position-2/": {
      "title": "Motorsport Management Adjunct Position",
      "description": "Motorsport Management Adjunct Position - Belmont Abbey College Skip to main content About Us About Us About Us Mission & vision Abbey News Leadership Monastery & Basilica Library Performing Arts Accreditation Belmont Abbey College The Catholic College of the South VISIT Academics Admissions APPLY GET INFO My abbey GIVE Motorsport Management Adjunct Position Home > About Us > Employment > Motorsport Management Adjunct Position Motorsport Management Adjunct Position Position Summary We are seeking highly qualified adjunct instructors to join our newly announced Master of Arts in Motorsport Management degree. Belmont Abbey College is now accepting applications for the Fall 2025 semester and future terms for the Master of Arts in Motorsport Management, which has received full approval from the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC). Job Responsibilities Candidates should have a proven track record of mentoring and developing emerging professionals, as well as strong research skills applicable to the field. Experience in directing student research projects or contributing to academic inquiry is highly valued. The role requires individuals who can integrate practical industry knowledge with academic rigor to provide students with a comprehensive and engaging learning experience. Qualifications Ideal candidates will possess a minimum of a graduate degree in business, sport management, or motorsport management related academic field. Ideal candidates would have 10 years of professional experience in the motorsport industry, demonstrating significant expertise in business-related roles and the management of teams, brands, or racing organizations. Application Process Fill out the following form to apply for one of Belmont Abbey College’s available academic positions. APPLY NOW Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the search is completed. Please apply by email to TreyCunningham@bac.edu using the subject line “Motorsport Management Adjunct.” Include a letter of application, vita, the names and contact information of at least three references, and a written response in which you explain how you might contribute to the College’s Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts mission, how your work engages with the Catholic intellectual tradition, or how your own faith tradition informs your vocation as teacher and scholar. Official transcripts are optional at this stage but are required for the interview. More From Our Motorsport Programs Motorsport Management Program Presents at Symposium 2025 July 21, 2026 Remembering Humpy Wheeler, Jr. August 21, 2025 Belmont Abbey College Welcomes Alums as Faculty for New Graduate Motorsport Management Program December 3, 2024 Belmont Abbey College Launches New Master of Arts in Motorsport Management Degree November 25, 2024 Patti Wheeler: Motorsports Pioneer August 14, 2024 Meet our Leadership Team Experienced, passionate and dedicated to the Benedictine spirit, the leadership team of the Abbey focuses on the academic, professional and spiritual growth of all students. See more Contact 100 Belmont-Mt. Holly Road Belmont, NC 28012 ADMISSIONS: 1-888-222-0110 FINANCIAL AID: 1-704-461-7000 MAIN NUMBER: 1-704-461-6700 FAX: 704-461-6220 info@bac.edu Quick Links DIRECTIONS TO THE COLLEGE SUPPORT THE COLLEGE TITLE IX CAMPUS DIRECTORY BELMONT ABBEY MONASTERY THE CATHOLIC SHOPPE CAMPUS SAFETY COLLEGE BOOKSTORE PRESS INQUIRIES ADMISSION INFORMATION VISIT CAMPUS MAP EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITIES PERFORMING ARTS 100 Belmont-Mt. Holly Road Belmont, NC 28012 ADMISSIONS: 1-888-222-0110 MAIN NUMBER: 1-704-461-6700 FAX: 704-461-6220 info@bac.edu Copyright ©2026 Belmont Abbey College | Minutes from Charlotte, we are ranked one of the top comprehensive colleges in the South by US News and World Report. Since 1876, the mission of Belmont Abbey College is the education of students from diverse religious, ethnic, and cultural backgrounds in the liberal a