    "https://belmontabbeycollege.edu/about-us/employment/financial-aid-counselor/": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor - Belmont Abbey College We use cookies to improve your experience. Please read our Privacy Policy or click Accept . Skip to main content About Us About Us About Us Mission & vision Abbey News Leadership Monastery & Basilica Library Performing Arts Accreditation Belmont Abbey College The Catholic College of the South Menu VISIT Academics Admissions APPLY GET INFO My abbey GIVE Financial Aid Counselor Home > About Us > Employment > Financial Aid Counselor Financial Aid Counselor Position Summary Belmont Abbey College seeks a self-motivated, customer service-oriented Financial Aid Counselor. Job Responsibilities The successful candidate plays a critical role in enabling students to realize their dream of a college education. The Counselor supports the Financial Aid Office in determining and providing financial assistance to students in accordance with college guidelines and in compliance with Federal and State regulations. The Counselor will package financial aid for students, certify loans, and generate award letters. The successful candidate will have or is willing to obtain Veterans Affairs certifying credentials to support students and families with VA benefits. Will assist with VA audit and other department projects. Working hours are 8:00 am to 5:00 pm, Monday through Friday. Some occasional weekend work is required. Qualifications The ideal candidate must have a Bachelor’s Degree. A minimum of two years financial aid experience is preferred. Candidate should be excited to support the division values of: Christ-like love for students, hospitality, and proactive and responsive communication. Must demonstrate knowledge in managing Title IV funds, counseling students and parents, and demonstrate commitment to excellence in delivering services to students. Comfortable speaking to students and families about financial aid areas. Experience with PowerFaids and/or Ellucian Colleague is preferred. Proficiency with Microsoft Office is required. The work environment is a general office setting with no strenuous physical demands. In addition, candidates must wholeheartedly embrace the mission of the College to educate students in the liberal arts and sciences so that in all things God may be glorified. The incumbent will consistently demonstrate skills, attitudes, and a stable disposition of character to support our Catholic and Benedictine identity while fostering the development of mind, body, and spirit in our students, our staff, and the greater community. Finally, candidates must have a sincere appreciation and acceptance of our Catholic approach to education and an understanding of Pope Saint John Paul II’s Ex corde Ecclesiae . Application Process Fill out the following form to apply for one of Belmont Abbey College’s available administrative positions. APPLY NOW Located ten minutes west of Charlotte, North Carolina, Belmont Abbey College is a Catholic, Benedictine school that educates a diverse student body in the liberal arts and sciences. The College, which is more than 130 years old, is known for its dedicated faculty, their excellent teaching, the personal attention that students receive, and a friendly atmosphere both inside and outside of the classroom.  There is a Benedictine monastery on campus, as well as a minor basilica.  In keeping with the monks’ age-old tradition of hospitality, the College community welcomes newcomers and works together for the benefit of our students–aiming to exemplify the aspiration that our College motto encapsulates: That in all things God may be glorified. Meet our Leadership Team Experienced, passionate and dedicated to the Benedictine spirit, the leadership team of the Abbey focuses on the academic, professional and spiritual growth of all students. See more Contact 100 Belmont-Mt. Holly Road Belmont, NC 28012 ADMISSIONS: 1-888-222-0110 FINANCIAL AID: 1-704-461-7000 MAIN NUMBER: 1-704-461-6700 FAX: 704-461-6220 info@bac.edu Quick Links DIRECTI